{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vj72RErbiJYTmkYNsdt5vL","type":"tool_result","content":"def branch_verdicts(root, base, rev):\n    \"\"\"The verdict paths whose bindings the branch changed between `base` and\n    `rev` - the adjudications this lane ran, through either route.\n\n    Implements: SR-232, LLR-310\n    \"\"\"\n    args = [\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--no-renames\", base, rev, \"--\", REVIEWS]\n    changed = (git_out(root, args) or \"\").splitlines()\n    return sorted(\n        p[: -len(REQUESTED_SUFFIX)] for p in changed if p.endswith(REQUESTED_SUFFIX)\n    )\n\n\ndef uncovered_refusal(root, base, rev, acts):\n    \"\"\"Why a merge must refuse the approval acts it adds, or None, WHETHER OR\n    NOT an act names a verdict (WI-841 round 14): every kind the acts take - a\n    flip needs `first-approval`, a re-attestation `amendment` - must be\n    covered by an ACCEPTED verdict (`accepted_at`) among the bindings this\n    branch carries (`branch_verdicts`), a combined sitting covering each kind\n    it requested. A lane whose only verdict for a kind is failed, pending,\n    invalid or unbound has no authority for that kind's act.\n\n    Implements: SR-232, LLR-310\n    \"\"\"\n    needed = {\n        kind\n        for act in acts\n        if isinstance(act, dict)\n        for key, kind in _ACT_KINDS\n        if act.get(key)\n    }\n    covered = set()\n    for verdict in branch_verdicts(root, base, rev) if needed else ():\n        covered |= set(accepted_at(root, rev, verdict) or {})\n    missing = sorted(needed - covered)\n    if not missing:\n        return None\n    return (\n        \"the adjudication's act takes {} with no ACCEPTED verdict of that kind \"\n        \"in this branch (each act is tied to its adjudication's accepted \"\n        \"verdict, named or not); nothing was merged. Remedy: re-sit the \"\n        \"adjudication through the loop or the coordinator's entry point, whose \"\n        \"binding records it accepted.\".format(\" and \".join(missing))\n    )\ndocs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/011-ADJUDICATE-c1d8dc6.md.requested\ndocs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/012-ADJUDICATE-327adae.md.requested\ndocs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/013-ADJUDICATE-37217b4.md.requested\ndocs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/014-ADJUDICATE-bac693c.md.requested\n== docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/011-ADJUDICATE-c1d8dc6.md.requested\nbrief = amendment\nkinds = amendment\n== docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/012-ADJUDICATE-327adae.md.requested\nbrief = amendment\nkinds = amendment\noutcome = accepted\n== docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/013-ADJUDICATE-37217b4.md.requested\nbrief = amendment\nkinds = amendment\noutcome = accepted\n== docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/014-ADJUDICATE-bac693c.md.requested\nbrief = amendment\nkinds = amendment\noutcome = accepted","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cffbbc6-0175-4e90-b9ab-7b165e0c0246","uuid":"743643e2-a363-4f84-a6a1-e7789be5551b","timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:53:15.696Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"def branch_verdicts(root, base, rev):\n    \"\"\"The verdict paths whose bindings the branch changed between `base` and\n    `rev` - the adjudications this lane ran, through either route.\n\n    Implements: SR-232, LLR-310\n    \"\"\"\n    args = [\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--no-renames\", base, rev, \"--\", REVIEWS]\n    changed = (git_out(root, args) or \"\").splitlines()\n    return sorted(\n        p[: -len(REQUESTED_SUFFIX)] for p in changed if p.endswith(REQUESTED_SUFFIX)\n    )\n\n\ndef uncovered_refusal(root, base, rev, acts):\n    \"\"\"Why a merge must refuse the approval acts it adds, or None, WHETHER OR\n    NOT an act names a verdict (WI-841 round 14): every kind the acts take - a\n    flip needs `first-approval`, a re-attestation `amendment` - must be\n    covered by an ACCEPTED verdict (`accepted_at`) among 