{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnfyQVACNRG8ECU3492z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three amended rows change meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=3`). I'd bless each new text, so I re-attested all three.\n\n**What changed:** every act an adjudication lane adds now needs an accepted verdict of each kind it takes, found among the verdict bindings the branch carries, even if the act names no verdict. A first approval needs an accepted first-approval verdict and a re-attestation needs an accepted amendment verdict. Before, an act that named no verdict was judged by the scope rules alone.\n- **LLR-278 and LLR-310:** they state that rule.\n- **TC-278:** every case that's expected to merge now carries an accepted binding of the right kind, and a new case shows that leaving out `--verdict` doesn't skip the check.\n\n**Why I'd bless them:** the code in `kitlib/sitting.py` matches, and `test_an_act_omitting_its_verdict_is_still_tied_to_an_accepted_one` tests the case where the verdict is left out.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `ff299523` — the verdict file `015-ADJUDICATE-58c7c11.md`, with the trailer `WI: WI-841`.\n- `bc47c087` — the re-attestation of all three rows, which copied both registries and recorded act seq 55 in the act ledger.\n\nThe pre-commit checks passed on both commits. The binding `015-ADJUDICATE-58c7c11.md.requested` is still untracked for the coordinator's outcome commit, as before.\n\n**The coordinator should check this before landing WI-841:** this lane's own merge will probably be refused under the rule I just blessed. I read the checker; I didn't run the merge check.\n- The branch's acts include two first approvals: act seq 47 (LLR-307, LLR-308, LLR-310, SR-232, TC-325, TC-327) and act seq 49 (TC-328).\n- The only verdict bindings the branch carries are for sittings 011–014. All four are amendment sittings, and 011's binding records no outcome at all.\n- So `uncovered_refusal` would fi